{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4694",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is implicated in the interaction with Ndufa1 through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12, a subunit of Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity, which is a critical component of the electron transport chain. This binding likely modulates the activity of the enzyme, influencing its role in cellular respiration. The presence of Ndufa1 as a participant in the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity further supports the notion that Metformin may regulate this metabolic process. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, biologically relevant relationship, suggesting that Metformin's interaction with Ndufa1 is mediated through the regulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Metformin influences cellular metabolism, potentially through the modulation of mitochondrial function.",
